AMLPSGG - Dataproc Multi-tenancy
Referencing the following setup https://docs.cloud.google.com/dataproc/docs/concepts/iam/sa-multi-tenancy#dataproc_create__multi_tenancy_cluster-gcloud
All test were conducted on qwiklab:
Create a workbench with a user account example user1 using the IAM service account:
 

Create an identity-config-file:

Create a identity-config.yaml file and place it in a GCS bucket

identity-config-file 
user_service_account_mapping:
  user1-simulated@example.com: user1-sa@qwiklabs-gcp-04-c5b46c1ff43b.iam.gserviceaccount.com
  user2-simulated@example.com: user2-sa@qwiklabs-gcp-04-c5b46c1ff43b.iam.gserviceaccount.com

Create a multitenant dataproc cluster (zero-scale):
Please note that the dataproc will have an additional role know as service account token creator
Dataproc multitenant zero-scale 
gcloud dataproc clusters create ac-cluster \
    --region=asia-southeast1 \
    --secure-multi-tenancy-user-mapping=ac-interactive@ac-project-485203.iam.gserviceaccount.com:ac-interactive@ac-project-485203.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
    --properties dataproc:dataproc.dynamic.multi.tenancy.enabled=true,core:fs.defaultFS=gs://team-485203 \
    --master-boot-disk-size 100GB \
    --worker-boot-disk-size 100GB \
    --cluster-type=zero-scale \
    --autoscaling-policy=zero-scale-policy \
    --master-machine-type "e2-standard-8" \
    --worker-machine-type "e2-standard-8” \
    --service-account=ac-spark@team-485203.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
    --optional-components=JUPYTER_KERNEL_GATEWAY \
    --enable-component-gateway

Create a multitenant dataproc cluster:
Please note that the dataproc will have an additional role know as service account token creator
create a multi-tenant dataproc cluster 
!gcloud dataproc clusters create "my-ac-cluster" \
    --region=us-central1 \
    --identity-config-file=gs://test-ac-bucket-1/config/user_mapping.yaml \
    --master-machine-type=e2-standard-8 \
    --master-boot-disk-size=30 \
    --worker-machine-type=e2-standard-8 \
    --worker-boot-disk-size=30 \
    --optional-components=JUPYTER_KERNEL_GATEWAY \
    --properties "dataproc:dataproc.dynamic.multi.tenancy.enabled=true" \
    --service-account=dataproc-test@qwiklabs-gcp-03-6e8213d90fd1.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
    --scopes=https://www.googleapis.com/auth/iam \
    --enable-component-gateway
 
Grant the necessary permissions to the user accounts:
Ensure user1 is granted the permissions to its own bucket example read write permissions to bucket.
 

